# CODEOWNERS — FinSoft
#
# Encodes the reviewers-by-tier table in docs/IMPLEMENTATION.md §10 and
# docs/OPERATING_MODEL.md §4 (ADR-0024). The tier is the highest one a PR
# touches; the comment above each block names its tier and Council seat.
#
#   T0  docs, copy, prototype UI        one peer agent
#   T1  normal UI/API behaviour         one peer agent (packages/ui: design-system)
#   T2  auth, tenancy, migrations, CI   Database/Security seat or Architecture seat
#   T3  posting, money, stock, tax      Accounting seat (+ Architecture for kernels)
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# READ THIS BEFORE TRUSTING IT AS A CONTROL
#
# Every owner below is @elitebytesolutions, the sole human maintainer. That is
# not a shortcut — it is an honest statement of what this file can currently
# enforce, which is *routing and visibility*, not independent approval.
#
# The reviewer names in IMPLEMENTATION.md — the Architecture, Accounting and
# Database/Security seats of the Technical Council, and the rest — are agent
# roles, not GitHub accounts. An agent has no GitHub identity, so it cannot be a code owner, and
# a guardian review is performed in-session and recorded in the PR rather than
# as a GitHub approval.
#
# GitHub also does not let an author approve their own pull request. While
# agents open PRs using the maintainer's account, the author and the only
# possible approver are the same identity, so required approvals are set to
# ZERO and required code-owner review is DISABLED. Any other setting
# deadlocks the repository rather than protecting it.
#
# Human-only merging is therefore PROCEDURAL, not an enforced security
# boundary. Credentials are shared with agents; the merge button is protected
# by discipline, not by GitHub.
#
# NOTHING BELOW IS CURRENTLY ENFORCED BY GITHUB.
#
# This repository is private on a Free plan, where branch protection,
# repository rulesets and secret scanning are all unavailable — verified, not
# assumed: the API returns 403 "Upgrade to GitHub Pro or make this repository
# public" for both branch protection and rulesets, and 422 "Secret scanning is
# not available for this repository".
#
# So required pull requests, required status checks, and blocked force pushes
# and deletions on main and develop are all currently unavailable. GitHub
# Actions IS enabled, so CI runs on every pull request and fails visibly — it
# simply cannot be made a merge requirement.
#
# Until that changes, this file routes and documents; it does not gate.
#
# Two things restore real enforcement:
#   - GitHub Pro on the account, which enables branch protection and rulesets;
#   - a separate GitHub App identity for agents, after which the author and
#     the approver differ, required approvals can be raised above zero, and
#     required code-owner review can be switched on.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

